{
  "_about": "Aki's streak mood for today, and its pose. `today.state` is the day verdict: studied (today counts, or will once unsent reviews arrive), protected, short (reviews short of the minimum), pending (no reviews) or unknown. `frozen_days` counts the heatmap's frozen days in a row ending yesterday (frozen_run). A counted day or a reached goal is fire, by heat: 1-6 aki_streak, 7-29 aki_streak_hot, 30-99 aki_streak_blazing, 100+ aki_streak_legend. Poses are Aki's; other companions map them to their own art. The desktop add-on (addon/moods.py, tests/test_streak_moods.py) checks it; the Android app keeps a copy for AnkiquestMood. `flames` is the flame beside the streak number for each mood (AnkiquestMood.flame): lit once today counts, unlit (grey) for a streak today has not counted for yet, icy (blue) when a freeze kept the days before today, none without a streak or when nothing is known about today. `messages` is the Today/Home line for a mood (AnkiquestAki.message, moods.mood), first match wins: sad is waiting; frozen_1-3 is freeze; every deck in `decks_due` done (none due, at least one deck) after `reviews` today is celebrate; cards due in the next deck (`focus_due`) is review; fire is streak; otherwise welcome. Review is a kind, not a line: clients show no line for it. The kinds are the add-on's names; Android's AnkiquestAki.Message calls celebrate COMPLETE and freeze PROTECTED.",
